=== ISSUE ===
Title: 188 tools is a lot of context for every session

Glama's review of this server (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/karayaman/lichess-mcp) says:

> With 88 tools, the count is excessive for the Lichess domain, leading to potential overwhelm and inefficiency. While the server covers many features, the high number suggests over-fragmentation, such as having separate tools for each tournament type (arena, swiss, simul) and multiple export functions, which could be consolidated.

The count is now 188. Their tools/list response is about 94,000 characters (very roughly 25-30k tokens), which the client sends to the model every session before the user asks anything. Most of it is for tournament organizers, bots and broadcasters.

Merging tools, as the review suggests, would cost schema clarity and the per-tool destructiveHint (an arena/swiss/simul tool would mix reads and destructive writes).

=== PR ===
Title: feat: enable a core set of tools by default, the rest via LICHESS_TOOLSETS
Body:
Closes #<issue>

- Tools are grouped by their existing source files into 22 toolsets.
- `LICHESS_TOOLSETS` picks them: unset or `core` gives 70 tools (account, users, relations, messaging, games, opening explorer, tablebase, puzzles, TV, analysis, the interactive UIs), about 34,000 characters instead of 94,000. `all` restores everything; `core,arena,swiss` adds to core.
- An unknown name stops the server at startup and lists the valid names.
- `buildServer(ctx, tools?)` still registers every tool when called without a selection.
- README: new Toolsets section; the Game Play and Tournaments examples note which toolsets they need.

**Behavior change:** without `LICHESS_TOOLSETS`, challenges, board play, tournaments, teams, studies, broadcasts, bots, bulk pairings and external engines are off. If you'd rather keep everything on by default, change the default to `all` in selectTools; the README table would change to match.

